  "notes": "{汚|よご}す is a transitive godan verb meaning \"to make dirty\" or \"to pollute.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {汚|よご}れる (intransitive - to get dirty)\n\nASPECT:\n- {汚|よご}している: is in the process of dirtying\n- {汚|よご}してある: has been intentionally dirtied\n\nCOMMON OBJECTS:\n- {服|ふく}を{汚|よご}す: to dirty clothes\n- {部屋|へや}を{汚|よご}す: to make a room messy\n- {空気|くうき}/{川|かわ}を{汚|よご}す: to pollute air/river\n- {名誉|めいよ}を{汚|よご}す: to tarnish one's honor\n\nIDIOM:\n{手|て}を{汚|よご}す has two meanings:\n1. Literal: to dirty one's hands\n2. Figurative: to do something immoral/criminal",
